<%# A word to a returning patron, inside the follow-up letter.

    Renamed from _wit_pride when the copy was genericized; the house copy it
    used to carry lives on verbatim as that house's theme override.

    Nothing to say to a first-timer, so nothing is printed: the generic house
    has no founding story, no awards and no neighbourhood to be proud of that
    this application could know about. Houses that do should override this
    partial in their theme.

    The letter is signed by the artistic director where there is one, so it
    speaks in the first person there and as the house otherwise. %>
<% visits = order.address.productions.count %>
<% if visits >= 2 %>
  <% personal = theater_info.first_person? %>
  <table class="w410" width="410" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0">
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td class="w410" width="410">
          <div align="left" class="article-content">
            <p>
              <%= personal ? 'I see' : 'We see' %> you've attended
              <%= pluralize visits, 'production' %> at <%= theater_info.name %>.
              Thank you — an audience that comes back is the whole point of the
              work we do here.
              <% if theater_info.default_theater&.accepts_donations %>
                If <%= theater_info.name %> has been important to you,
                <%= personal ? "I'd" : "we'd" %> like to invite you to
                <a href="<%= new_donation_url %>">support the theater and our mission</a><% if theater_info.phone.present? %>
                  or give <%= personal ? 'me' : 'us' %> a call at <%= theater_info.phone %><% end %>.
              <% end %>
            </p>
          </div>
        </td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
<% end %>
